Just so we're all clear: the essay is *NOT* a formal proposal, of
anything.  It was made to see what the community thinks of the
direction I was heading in.

Since the community has overwhelmingly said they are interested, the
BPFK and I will produce a real proposal.  It will include a real,
serious, set of goals.  Those may not be the same as what's in my
essay.  In particular, Jorge thinks (loosely) that past usage and
awesomeness should be equal priority, and Jorge almost always
manages to convince me he's right in the end (because he's really
smart :).

I have absolutely no intention of producing a structure that will
allow any random kook to radically modify the language.  (I am
seriously pissed that anyone would believe that I and the rest of
the community would allow such a thing, but cooler heads have
prevailed to make this email not the extremely angry rant it started
out as.)

We (the current BPFK) will get back to y'all with something real,
hopefully shortly.

-Robin

